meta {
  name: Get My Master Profile
  type: http
  seq: 1
}

get {
  url: {{base_url}}/api/v1/master/me
  body: none
  auth: bearer
}

auth:bearer {
  token: {{token}}
}

headers {
  Accept: application/json
  X-Locale: {{locale}}
}

script:post-response {
  if (res.status === 200) {
    bru.setVar("master_id", res.body.data.id);
  }
}

docs {
  # Get Master Profile

  First call of the master side — the **same** `{{token}}` as everywhere else.
  The `ensure.master` middleware resolves the master profile behind the client
  account and hands it to the controller, so no separate master login exists.

  Saves the profile id into `{{master_id}}` for the location endpoint.

  **Response 200:**
  ```json
  {
    "data": {
      "id": 1,
      "name": "Aydogdy Ussadow",
      "phone": "+99362111222",
      "is_active": true,
      "is_available": true,
      "access_expires_at": "2026-12-31",
      "experience_years": 8,
      "about": "Сантехник с 2017 года.",
      "city": { "id": 1, "name": "Ашхабад" },
      "categories": [{ "id": 1, "name": "Сантехника" }]
    }
  }
  ```

  | Field              | Description                                      |
  |--------------------|--------------------------------------------------|
  | `is_active`        | Not blocked by the administrator                 |
  | `is_available`     | Set by the master — ready for work right now     |
  | `access_expires_at`| When the subscription runs out                   |
  | `experience_years` | Editable by the master — see Update Master Profile |
  | `about`            | Editable by the master, may be `null`            |

  **403 — read the `reason`:** `not_a_master`, `application_pending`,
  `application_rejected`, `disabled`, `access_expired`. See the collection docs
  for what each one means.
}
